  m237f2c82faf9 "Links theory in four symbols"
  m949a0cb8187b "All PDFs (ZIP)"
  m8dedf7ef0b06 "Versions of the links theory"
  m22c5a1565ce7 "Each symbol is one network of links, and each link is one unbroken line in its own colour: a bar marks its source, an arrow its target, and its middle is the point other links refer to. Link 0 (0: 0 0) is “nothing”: it always exists and is never drawn, so a reference to 0 is a free end, and a link that refers to itself twice is a figure eight. These networks are also the alphabet of the rain in the background."
